@@ -92,3 +96,15 @@ A tree export is insufficient: it omits tokens and internal continuation state.
 Filesystem atomicity belongs to the CLI; concurrent writers require application
 coordination. A crash may leave an uncommitted tree export, but the old model file
 remains usable until the state rename succeeds.
+
+## CSV application identities
+
+CLI conversion trims nonempty URLs and prefixes them with `url:`. URL-less rows
+receive `csv-row:<conversion UUID>:<batch index>:<row number>`, so independently
+converted files cannot share fallback identities. The saved SourceBatch JSON is
+the replay artifact: reconverting CSV creates fresh URL-less identities and does
+not deduplicate the same anonymous article across conversions. URL identity does
+not canonicalize URL aliases or track lifetime duplicates after gamma expiration.
+CSV timestamps accept RFC3339 or space-separated dates with explicit numeric
+UTC offsets; malformed and timezone-free values remain unset. These are ingestion
+contracts, not algorithmic time or forgetting rules.
